          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi R
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p R q
            and the truth of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mi R
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q R p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi R
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p R q
            is this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
            on odd
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is a square
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+arithmetic"} modulo
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
          %p
            The law of quadratic reciprocity is a celebrated result due to
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss"} Gauss
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+field+theory"} class field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} primes
            decompose in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+extension"} abelian extensions
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+fields"} number fields
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \geq 1
            an odd
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %strong Legendre symbol
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em quadratic reciprocity symbol
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{a}{p}\right)
            to be the unique element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-1, 0, 1\}
            for which
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(\frac{a}{p}\right) \equiv a^{\frac{p-1}{2}} \; mod \; p
          %p
            Notice that the Legendre symbol defines a surjective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/p)^\ast \cong C_{p-1} \to \{-1, 1\}
          %p
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            is the set of squares in the multiplicative group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/p)^\ast
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{a}{p}\right) = 1
            means
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is a square modulo
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{a}{p}\right) = -1
            means
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is a non-square modulo
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_quadratic_reciprocity Theorem (Quadratic Reciprocity)
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              distinct odd primes,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi p
                        %mi q
                      %mo )
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi q
                        %mi p
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi q
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{p}{q}\right) \left(\frac{q}{p}\right) = (-1)^{\frac{p-1}{2}\frac{q-1}{2}}.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 2
                        %mi p
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{2}{p}\right) = (-1)^{\frac{p^2-1}{8}}
            %p
              i.e.,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              is a square modulo
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              if and only if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo ±
                      %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mod
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 8
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \equiv \pm 1 \; mod \; 8
          %p
            The case for odd primes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            can be restated as:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q
                are odd and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ≡
                        %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi mod
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \equiv 1 \; mod \; 4
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mi p
                          %mi q
                        %mo )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mi q
                          %mi p
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{p}{q}\right) = \left(\frac{q}{p}\right)
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo ≡
                      %mn 3
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mod
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q \equiv 3 \; mod \; 4
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mi p
                          %mi q
                        %mo )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mi q
                          %mi p
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{p}{q}\right) = -\left(\frac{q}{p}\right)
          %p
            The law of quadratic reciprocity was first fully proven by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Gauss"} Gauss
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermat"} Fermat
            (who effectively realized when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
            was a square modulo
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            based on his
            %span.newWikiWord
              two squares theorem
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/two+squares+theorem"} ?
            – well before Legendre introduced his eponymous symbol), and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler"} Euler
            (who proved the case for
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = 2
          %p
            None of these early authors were in full possession of modern notations such as the congruence symbol or the Legendre symbol, which greatly economize the amount of thought needed to prove this theorem. Recognition of quadratic reciprocity was likely rooted in empirical observations, for example the study of periods of expansions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/q
            in base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            (source?).
          %h2#sample_classroom_application Sample classroom application
          %p
            Consider the problem of computing the length of the period of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 65537
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/65537
            in its decimal expansion. This period is the same as the least positive exponent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 10
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≡
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 65537
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 10^n \equiv 1 \; mod \; 65537
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 65536
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 65536
            (thus, a power of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 65537
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 65537
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermat+prime"} Fermat prime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mn 4
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{2^4} + 1
          %p
            The period is a proper divisor of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 65536
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 65536
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 10
            is a square modulo
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 65537
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 65537
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 10
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 5
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{10}{p}\right) = \left(\frac{2}{p}\right) \left(\frac{5}{p}\right)
          %p
            where the first factor is pretty clearly
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            (already
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mn 32
                    %mo ≡
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{32} \equiv 1 \; mod \; p
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ≡
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{\frac{p-1}{2}} \equiv 1 \; mod \; p
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 5
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi p
                      %mn 5
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 2
                      %mn 5
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{5}{p}\right) = \left(\frac{p}{5}\right) = \left(\frac{2}{5}\right) = -1
          %p
            and we therefore conclude
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 10
            is a non-square modulo
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 65537
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 65537
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 65537
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/65537
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 65536
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 65536
          %h2#proofs Proofs
          %p There are today several hundred published proofs of the quadratic reciprocity laws; it is rightly regarded as a capstone result in undergraduate introductions to number theory. We give two proofs here.
          %h3#proof_via_gauss_sums Proof via Gauss sums
          %p
            This proof, following
            %a{:href => "#Lang"} Lang
            (pp. 76–78), is middling in sophistication but at least indicates the relevance of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclotomic+extension"} cyclotomic extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            and
            = succeed "s" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                quadratic extension
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/quadratic+extension"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            be a fixed odd prime, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ζ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta
            be a primitive
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{th}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/root+of+unity"} root of unity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character"} character
            sum called a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss+sum"} Gauss sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi a
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                    %mo )
                  %msup
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \coloneqq \sum_a \left(\frac{a}{p}\right) \zeta^a,
          %p
            where the sum is over non-zero elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                        %mi p
                      %mo )
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 = \left(\frac{-1}{p}\right) p
              \.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                          %mi p
                        %mo )
                      %msup
                        %mi ζ
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 = \sum_{a, b} \left(\frac{a b}{p}\right) \zeta^{a + b}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              ranges over all non-zero residue classes, so does
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b
              to get
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo ,
                                %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mi b
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %msup
                              %mi ζ
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo +
                                %mi a
                                %mi b
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo ,
                                %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi b
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %msup
                              %mi ζ
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %mi b
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %msup
                              %mi ζ
                              %mn 0
                            %mo +
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi b
                                %mo ≠
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi b
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mi a
                            %msup
                              %mi ζ
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %mi b
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^2 &amp; = &amp; \sum_{a, b} \left(\frac{a^2 b}{p}\right) \zeta^{a + a b} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; \sum_{a, b} \left(\frac{b}{p}\right) \zeta^{a(1 + b)} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; \sum_a \left(\frac{-1}{p}\right) \zeta^0 + \sum_{b \neq -1} \left(\frac{b}{p}\right) \sum_a \zeta^{a(1 + b)}
                    }.
            %p
              Now, for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≠
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \neq -1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mi ζ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_a \zeta^{a(1+b)}
              evaluates to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
              since
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi ζ
                      %mo +
                      %mi …
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi ζ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 + \zeta + \ldots + \zeta^{p-1} = 0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi b
                                %mo ≠
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi b
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi b
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^2 &amp; = &amp; \left(\frac{-1}{p}\right) (p-1) + (-1)\sum_{b \neq -1} \left(\frac{b}{p}\right) \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; \left(\frac{-1}{p}\right) p - \sum_b \left(\frac{b}{p}\right) \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; \left(\frac{-1}{p}\right) p
                    }
            %p which completes the proof.
          %p
            Thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            belongs to a quadratic extension of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msqrt
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{p})
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{-p})
            depending on the Legendre symbol. In particular, the prime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ramification"} ramified
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ζ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}(\zeta)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_quadratic_reciprocity_law Proof of quadratic reciprocity law
            %p
              First let
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              be two distinct odd primes. With
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              defined as above, we calculate
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi q
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mod
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^q \; mod \; q
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} mod \; q
              indicates the quotient of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              generated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              in the above-mentioned quadratic extension of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %p On the one hand, by the preceding lemma,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi q
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mi p
                                %mo )
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi q
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi q
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi q
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi q
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≡
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi q
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi p
                                %mi q
                              %mo )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi q
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^q &amp; = &amp; S(S^2)^{\frac{q-1}{2}} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; S\left(\frac{-1}{p}\right)^{\frac{q-1}{2}} p^{\frac{q-1}{2}} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; S(-1)^{\frac{p-1}{2}\frac{q-1}{2}} p^{\frac{q-1}{2}} \\
                    \&amp; \equiv &amp; S (-1)^{\frac{p-1}{2}\frac{q-1}{2}} \left(\frac{p}{q}\right) \; mod \; q
                    \.}
            %p
              On the other hand, since raising to the power
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} automorphism
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              obtained modulo
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              (either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi q
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_q \times \mathbb{F}_q
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi q
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_{q^2}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a square modulo
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              or not), we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≡
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi a
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %msup
                              %mi ζ
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mi q
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≡
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi q
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi a
                                  %mi q
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %msup
                              %mi ζ
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mi q
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≡
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mi q
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %mi S
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^q &amp; \equiv &amp; \sum_a \left(\frac{a}{p}\right) \zeta^{a q} \; mod \; q \\
                    \&amp; \equiv &amp; \left(\frac{q}{p}\right) \sum_a \left(\frac{a q}{p}\right) \zeta^{a q} \; mod \; q \\
                    \&amp; \equiv &amp; \left(\frac{q}{p}\right) S \; mod \; q
                    }
            %p
              and now we can cancel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              (which is invertible modulo
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
              is) to arrive at
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi q
                        %mi p
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi q
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi p
                        %mi q
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{q}{p}\right) = (-1)^{\frac{p-1}{2}\frac{q-1}{2}} \left(\frac{p}{q}\right)
            %p which gives the first clause of the reciprocity law.
            %p
              As for the second clause, we can give a similar analysis. The prime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = 2
              is ramified in the cyclotomic extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}[i]
              since
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi i
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 + i)^2 = 2 i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              we may calculate
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 + i)^p \; mod \; p
              in two ways. On the one hand,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %mi i
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mi i
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≡
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 2
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (1 + i)^p &amp; = &amp; (1+i)(2 i)^{\frac{p-1}{2}} \\
                    \&amp; \equiv &amp; (1+i)i^{\frac{p-1}{2}} \left(\frac{2}{p}\right) \; mod \; p
                    }
            %p and on the other hand,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %mi i
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≡
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mn 1
                              %mi p
                            %mo +
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mi p
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (1+i)^p &amp; \equiv &amp; 1^p + i^p \; mod \; p
                    }
            %p
              and by examining the cases
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≡
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 5
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 7
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \equiv 1, 3, 5, 7 \; mod \; 8
              separately, we easily deduce the second clause.
          %h3#zolotarevs_proof Zolotarev’s proof
          %p
            The (in hindsight obvious!) structural meaning of the Legendre symbol was first given by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Zolotarev"} Zolotarev
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_zolotarev Lemma (Zolotarev)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              an odd prime and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              relatively prime to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi a
                        %mi p
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{a}{p}\right)
              is the sign or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+permutation"} signature of a permutation
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p
              given by multiplying by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            is the unique fixed point of this permutation, this statement is equivalent to the same statement but with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p
            replaced by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/p)^\ast
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Both the Legendre symbol
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{ }{p}\right) \colon (\mathbb{Z}/p)^\ast \to \{-1, 1\}
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Cayley
                    %mi Perm
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi sign
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/p)^\ast \stackrel{Cayley}{\to} Perm((\mathbb{Z}/p)^\ast) \stackrel{sign}{\to} \{-1, 1\}
            %p
              are homomorphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/root#roots_of_unity_in_fields_11"} whose domain is a cyclic group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cayley
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cayley(g)
              is a cyclic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p-1
              elements, hence has sign
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{p-2} = -1
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mi g
                          %mi p
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{g}{p}\right)
          %p
            We turn now to Zolotarev’s proof of the “hard” case of quadratic reciprocity where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            are distinct odd primes. What is interesting is that from this point forward, we don’t use primality of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            at all, i.e., the remainder of the argument carries over if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            are replaced by odd, relatively prime integers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{a}{n}\right)
            as a sign of a permutation of multiplying by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/n
            %strong Jacobi symbol
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi i
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\frac{a}{n}\right) \coloneqq \prod_{i} \left(\frac{a}{p_i}\right)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mi …
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = p_1 \ldots p_r
            is the prime factorization of an odd integer, and what we really do is generalize quadratic reciprocity from the Legendre symbol to the Jacobi symbol. Thus, the primality assumption is concentrated purely in the preceding lemma.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_quadratic_reciprocity Proof of quadratic reciprocity
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \gt 1
              an odd number, we consider the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi m
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/m = \{0, 1, \ldots, m-1\}
              as carrying on the one hand a ring structure, and on the other as carrying a structure of linear order (no compatibility between these structures!). Now suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              are odd and relatively prime; then by the
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Chinese remainder theorem
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Chinese+remainder+theorem"} ?
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/m n \to \mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n.
            %p
              If we endow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n
              with the dictionary or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lexicographic+order"} lexicographic order
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+orders"} total orders
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Dict
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n)_{Dict} \to \mathbb{Z}/m n
            %p
              which takes an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \in \mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi m
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n x + y \in \{0, 1, \ldots, m n - 1\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              columns and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              cards in each column, into a single stack of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m n
              cards, by gathering up the first column, followed by gathering up the second column and placing it underneath, etc.)
            %p
              The composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              of the functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Dict
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi ord
                        %mo ≅
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi ring
                        %mo ≅
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n)_{Dict} \stackrel{ord \cong}{\to} \mathbb{Z}/m n \stackrel{ring \cong}{\to} \mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n
            %p
              is thus
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi n
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \mapsto n x + y \mapsto (n x + y, y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              row permutations, one for each fixed
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in row
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is taken to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n x + y
              in row
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi n
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto n x + y
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sign
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi sign
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi sign
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi n
                        %mi m
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sign((-) + y) \cdot sign(n(-)) = sign(n(-)) = \left(\frac{n}{m}\right)
            %p
              (since the permutation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) + y
              is a cyclic permutation on an odd number of elements, hence is even). Thus
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sign
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mi n
                          %mi m
                        %mo )
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi n
                        %mi m
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sign(\alpha) = \left(\frac{n}{m}\right)^n = \left(\frac{n}{m}\right)
            %p
              where the second equation follows since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is odd.
            %p
              Similarly, consider
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n
              with the
              %em reverse
              dictionary order, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \lt (x', y')
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \lt y'
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = y'
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt x'
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi RevDict
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi ord
                        %mo ≅
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi ring
                        %mo ≅
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n)_{RevDict} \stackrel{ord \cong}{\to} \mathbb{Z}/m n \stackrel{ring \cong}{\to} \mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n,
            %p
              as taking
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi m
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \mapsto (x, x + m y)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sign
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi m
                        %mi n
                      %mo )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sign(\beta) = \left(\frac{m}{n}\right).
            %p
              Finally,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi β
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta^{-1} \circ \alpha
              is the unique order-preserving isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Dict
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi RevDict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n)_{Dict} \to (\mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n)_{RevDict}
            %p
              which gives a permutation on the underlying set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi m
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                            %mn 2
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{\frac{m-1}{2}\frac{n-1}{2}}
            %p
              But this is easy to see. Recall that given a permutation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              on a linearly ordered set (such as
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi m
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Dict
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/m \times \mathbb{Z}/n)_{Dict}
              %em inversion
              is a pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \lt y)
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(x) \gt \sigma(y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I(\sigma)
              is the total number of inversions, then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} sign
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sign(\sigma) = (-1)^{I(\sigma)}.
            %p
              In the present case
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi β
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma = \beta^{-1} \alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I(\sigma)
              counts pairs of pairs
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, j)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i', j')
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, j) \lt (i', j')
              in dictionary order but
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, j) \gt (i', j')
              in reverse dictionary order; in other words when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi i
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \lt i'
              but
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ′
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j' \lt j
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi m
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I(\sigma) = \frac{m(m-1)}{2} \frac{n(n-1)}{2}
            %p
              whence (again since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m, n
              are odd)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{I(\sigma)} = (-1)^{\frac{m-1}{2}\frac{n-1}{2}}
            %p which completes the proof.
          %h2#other_reciprocity_laws Other reciprocity laws
          %p
            As mentioned earlier, quadratic reciprocity law is due to Gauss and is the first of a number of reciprocity laws in number theory. The Wikipedia article lists a bevy of reciprocity laws, gradually increasing in modernity and abstraction (and power), and culminating in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+reciprocity"} Artin reciprocity
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+field+theory"} class field theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss+sum"} Gauss sum
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "Jacobi+theta+function#FunctionalEquation"} Jacobi theta function – Functional equation and Reciprocity
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Lang
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serge+Lang"}> Serge Lang
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic number theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 110
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0853-2"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-0853-2
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reciprocity_law_%28mathematics%29"} Reciprocity laws (mathematics)
            %li#Gauss
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carl+Friedrich+Gauss"}> Carl Friedrich Gauss
                ,
                %em Disquisitiones arithmeticae
                (1801), Article IV.
            %li#Zolotarev
              %p
                E.I. Zolotareff,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nouvelle démonstration de la loi de de réciprocité de Legendre
            %li#Casselman11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Casselman"}> Bill Casselman
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dirichlet’s calculation of Gauss sums
                %strong 2
                57 (2011) 281–301 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://content.ems.press/assets/public/full-texts/serials/lem/57/3/12115/online/10.4171-lem-57-3-2.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Casselman-DirichletGaussSum.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
